So at 12 midnight I wrapped up a very successful hacking session: my orc 
barbarian had obtained Cleaver, was in good standing with Set, and had 
reached the castle to retrieve the WoW. With -18 AC and about 140 hp I 
decided the next step would be to undertake the quest, build up my hp, 
AC and stats (and add some things to my inventory along the way) and 
then, at the appropriate moment, undertake an ascension run.

But for some reason I couldn't go to sleep. So I got up at 2 am and 
started playing again. And that's when everything went wrong. I was 
inexplicably crowned and proceeded to make Set angry (probably bumping 
into too many peaceful creatures with Stormbringer). And how did I 
discover he was peaved? AFTER I had donned a cursed blindfold.

I got into Set's good graces after a sacfest at an altar. And for some 
inconceivable reason I proceeded to cease caring about the game - 
probably thanks to the time of night. I know, for instance, that 
meleeing with giant eels is a bad thing. But I wanted to see if I could 
get away with it. I did, in fact.

What I didn't get away with was meleeing with the mind flayer that ate 
my brain, which was no surprise because I hadn't bothered to wear a 
helmet. I could have done any number of things to escape the mind 
flayer, but did not - oh well. Set was angry at me again anyways...

